          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homeowners coating a garage themselves, Rust-Oleum's EpoxyShield Professional kit is the practical choice, with RockSolid as the faster-turnaround option and Leggari's polyaspartic for those who want the most durable DIY floor and can work quickly. ArmorPoxy suits heavy-use shops, Granite Grip suits foot-traffic outdoor slabs, and Siloxa-Tek protects concrete without any coating at all.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, the system will only be as good as the slab beneath it. Test for sealers and moisture, grind or etch to the profile the manufacturer specifies, mix in batches you can spread, and give each layer its full cure. Get those steps right and a coated floor can look sharp and stay bonded for a decade.
